cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this corpus or result, please cite it as below."
title: "SlopCheck: a labelled corpus of 557 curl security reports and a negative result on source-tree grounding"
abstract: >-
  A labelled corpus of 557 publicly disclosed curl security reports (126
  maintainer-confirmed vulnerabilities, 49 from curl's published AI-slop
  archive), and a measurement showing that grounding a vulnerability report's
  stated facts against the project's source tree does not separate genuine
  reports from fabricated ones. The finished checker scores Youden J = 0.083
  against a median noise floor of 0.092.
authors:
